  "id": "applied-relaxation",
  "term": "applied relaxation",
  "definition": "Applied relaxation is a behavioral mental health technique that teaches people to notice early signs of tension or stress and relax quickly in response. It usually builds from progressive muscle relaxation practice toward using brief relaxation in imagined and real stressful situations, with the goal of carrying the skill into everyday life.",
